"},{"path":"harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md","content":"# Task: E01 reliability aggregation

## Objective

Extend the existing Agent Dev benefit evaluation report with deterministic repeated-trial aggregation without creating a new metrics platform.

## Contract

- Reuse `shared/agent-dev/scenarios.ts` as the scenario registry and `shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json` as the registered deterministic oracle.
- Register `k`, `minCases`, and the flake threshold in the fixture before evaluation.
- The design sample gate is `k = 3` and at least 20 complete cases.
- Aggregate pass^k (all k trials pass), pass@k (at least one trial passes), per-trial success rate, and flake rate.
- A case is incomplete when any trial is missing, timed out, crashed, or skipped. Preserve every such case and exclude it from case metric denominators.
- A flake has a failed first trial and a successful later fixed retry. Preserve that first failure; a retry does not repair the original gate failure.
- Positive anchors must pass every trial. Negative anchors must reject every trial. Any anchor violation fails the gate.
- Safety-required cases permit no skip and no flake.
- If the complete sample does not meet the design gate, report `insufficient-sample`; never report a small sample as pass.
- Report raw and complete denominators separately, including incomplete counts and reasons.
- The fixture is a deterministic internal oracle, not evidence of real-provider behavior, human approval, or unseen-model generalization.

## Acceptance

The generated JSON and Markdown benefit reports expose both pass^k and pass@k without conflating them, retain incomplete cases, and derive the gate deterministically.
"},{"path":"harness/specs/rules/reliability-aggregation-boundary.md","content":"# Reliability aggregation boundary

1. Reliability aggregation is an internal evaluation-report feature. It must not change product defaults, product locks, approval semantics, or user-visible configuration.
2. The implementation must reuse the Agent Dev benefit evaluator and existing scenario registry. It must not introduce a separate metrics service, product dependency, timer, or automation.
3. `pass^k` means all k trials of a complete case passed. `pass@k` means at least one of the k trials passed. Their names, values, and denominators must remain distinct.
4. Missing, timeout, crash, and skip are explicit incomplete outcomes. Incomplete cases remain visible but are excluded from complete-case metric denominators.
5. Flake detection uses the first trial and later fixed retries. The original failure remains recorded. Safety-required cases have zero skip and zero flake requirements.
6. Positive anchors require all-trial pass; negative anchors require all-trial reject. A violation is a gate failure.
7. Fewer than 20 complete cases, or a k other than 3, is `insufficient-sample`, not pass.
8. Registered fixture data is a deterministic oracle. Reports must not imply real-provider performance, human validation, or generalization to unseen models.
9. Reports must disclose the raw denominator, complete denominator, pass^k, pass@k, per-trial success rate, flake rate, incomplete counts, gate, and reasons.
"},{"path":"docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md","content":"# E01 — deterministic reliability aggregation

## Scope

This closure adds internal repeated-trial aggregation to the existing Agent Dev benefit report. It does not add a user-visible interface, configuration, product default, product lock, approval behavior, dependency, or scheduled automation. README files therefore require no change.

## Design

The deterministic oracle is `shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json`, linked to the existing Agent Dev scenario registry. The fixture registers `k = 3`, `minCases = 20`, and `flakeThreshold = 0.05` before evaluation.

The aggregator reports:

- raw case denominator and complete-case denominator;
- pass^k: complete cases whose every trial passed;
- pass@k: complete cases with at least one passing trial;
- per-trial success rate;
- flake rate: a failed first trial followed by a successful fixed retry;
- explicit missing, timeout, crash, and skip case counts;
- positive and negative anchor results;
- safety-required skip and flake counts;
- gate and machine-readable reasons.

Incomplete cases are retained in the report and excluded from complete-case denominators. A first failure is never erased by a successful retry. Anchor violations and safety violations fail the gate. A sample with fewer than 20 complete cases at k=3 is `insufficient-sample`.

## Verification record

The clean-candidate fast gate covers directed unit tests, runtime/core type checking, scoped lint, and harness validation/dry-run. Credential scanning must report zero hits and `SHA256SUMS` must be readable. This is an acceptance record rather than a product README change because the package has no user-visible API or configuration change.

## Interpretation boundary

The fixture is a deterministic internal oracle. It is not a claim about a real provider, a human reviewer, or generalization to unseen models.
"},{"path":"scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs","content":"#!/usr/bin/env node
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import { mkdir, readFile, readdir, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';
import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks';
import { aggregateReliability } from './lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs';

const ROOT = process.cwd();
const OUT_DIR = resolve(ROOT, 'artifacts/agent-dev-benefit-eval');

async function read(path) {
  return await readFile(resolve(ROOT, path), 'utf8');
}

async function walk(dir, predicate = () => true) {
  const results = [];
  async function visit(abs) {
    for (const entry of await readdir(abs, { withFileTypes: true })) {
      if (entry.name === 'node_modules' || entry.name === '.git' || entry.name === 'dist') continue;
      const full = join(abs, entry.name);
      if (entry.isDirectory()) await visit(full);
      else if (predicate(full)) results.push(full);
    }
  }
  await visit(resolve(ROOT, dir));
  return results;
}

function countMatches(text, pattern) {
  return [...text.matchAll(pattern)].length;
}

function extractScenarioIds(registryText) {
  const match = registryText.match(/export const AGENT_DEV_SCENARIOS = \[([\s\S]*?)\] as const/);
  return match ? [...match[1].matchAll(/\{\s*id:\s*'([^']+)'/g)].map((entry) => entry[1]) : [];
}

function packageInstalled(name) {
  const normalized = name.startsWith('@')\ ? name.replace('/', '\\') : name;
  return existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'node_modules', ...normalized.split(/[\\/]/)));
}

async function scanSelectorCoverage() {
  const files = await walk('src', (file) => /\.(tsx|ts)$/.test(file));
  let testIdCount = 0;
  let interactiveTagCount = 0;
  let interactiveWithoutInlineTestId = 0;
  for (const file of files) {
    const text = await readFile(file, 'utf8');
    testIdCount += countMatches(text, /data-testid=/g);
    const tags = [...text.matchAll(/<(?<tag>button|input|select|textarea|a)\b(?<attrs>[^>]*)>/g)];
    interactiveTagCount += tags.length;
    interactiveWithoutInlineTestId += tags.filter((match) => !String(match.groups?.attrs ?? '').includes('data-testid')).length;
  }
  return {
    fileCount: files.length,
    testIdCount,
    interactiveTagCount,
    interactiveWithoutInlineTestId,
    inlineSelectorCoverage: interactiveTagCount === 0 ? 1 : Number(((interactiveTagCount - interactiveWithoutInlineTestId) / interactiveTagCount).toFixed(3)),
  };
}

function formatRate(value) {
  return value === null ? 'not available' : `${(value * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
}

function renderMarkdown(report) {
  const tools = report.externalTools.map((tool) => (
    `| ${tool.package} | ${tool.installed ? 'yes' : 'no'} | ${tool.role} |`
  )).join('\n');
  const reliability = report.reliability;
  const incomplete = reliability.incompleteCounts;
  const reasons = reliability.reasons.length > 0
    ? reliability.reasons.map((item) => `- \`${item.code}\`: ${item.message}`).join('\n')
    : '- None.';
  return `# Agent Dev Benefit Evaluation

Generated: ${report.generatedAt}

## Summary

| Metric | Value |
| --- | ---: |
| Dev scenarios | ${report.agentDev.scenarioCount} |
| hostApi.agentDev methods | ${report.agentDev.hostApiMethodCount} |
| E2E agent-dev helpers | ${report.agentDev.e2eHelperCount} |
| Runtime schema assertions | ${report.agentDev.schemaAssertionCount} |
| Basic a11y rule families | ${report.quality.a11yRuleCount} |
| Renderer files scanned | ${report.selectorCoverage.fileCount} |
| data-testid occurrences | ${report.selectorCoverage.testIdCount} |
| Interactive tags scanned | ${report.selectorCoverage.interactiveTagCount} |
| Inline selector coverage | ${Math.round(report.selectorCoverage.inlineSelectorCoverage * 100)}% |

## External Tool Readiness

| Package | Installed | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
${tools}

## Deterministic Reliability Aggregation

Oracle: **${reliability.oracle}**. This fixture is not evidence of a real provider, human validation, or unseen-model generalization.

| Metric | Value |
| --- | ---: |
| Registered k | ${reliability.k} |
| Registered minimum complete cases | ${reliability.minCases} |
| Raw case denominator | ${reliability.rawCaseCount} |
| Complete case denominator | ${reliability.completeCaseCount} |
| pass^k (all k trials pass) | ${formatRate(reliability.passPowerK)} |
| pass@k (at least one trial passes) | ${formatRate(reliability.passAtK)} |
| Per-trial success rate | ${formatRate(reliability.trialSuccessRate)} |
| Flake rate | ${formatRate(reliability.flakeRate)} |
| Missing cases | ${incomplete.missing} |
| Timeout cases | ${incomplete.timeout} |
| Crash cases | ${incomplete.crash} |
| Skip cases | ${incomplete.skip} |
| Positive anchors passed | ${reliability.anchors.positive.passed}/${reliability.anchors.positive.total} |
| Negative anchors passed | ${reliability.anchors.negative.passed}/${reliability.anchors.negative.total} |
| Gate | **${reliability.gate}** |

### Gate reasons

${reasons}

## Interpretation

- The current in-repo implementation already gives agents ${report.agentDev.scenarioCount} deterministic page entry points and ${report.agentDev.e2eHelperCount} E2E helpers without depending on new packages.
- Schema assertions now reject malformed agent-dev payloads at the Main host-api boundary.
- Basic a11y and visual artifact generation are available through Playwright today; axe/Argos can replace the fallback scanners once supply-chain policy allows installing them.
- The selector coverage metric is a heuristic. It is useful as a trend line, not as a precise accessibility or E2E quality proof.
- pass^k and pass@k are separate metrics. Incomplete cases remain recorded but are excluded from their complete-case denominators.
`;
}

const start = performance.now();
const [
  scenarioRegistry,
  hostApi,
  e2eFixture,
  schemaText,
  a11yText,
  reliabilityFixtureText,
] = await Promise.all([
  read('shared/agent-dev/scenarios.ts'),
  read('src/lib/host-api.ts'),
  read('tests/e2e/fixtures/electron.ts'),
  read('shared/host-api/agent-dev-schemas.ts'),
  read('tests/e2e/fixtures/a11y.ts'),
  read('shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json'),
]);

const scenarioIds = extractScenarioIds(scenarioRegistry);
const hostApiAgentDevBlock = hostApi.match(/agentDev:\s*\{([\s\S]*?)\n  \},\n  providers:/)?.[1] ?? '';
const report = {
  generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  durationMs: 0,
  agentDev: {
    scenarioCount: scenarioIds.length,
    scenarios: scenarioIds,
    hostApiMethodCount: countMatches(hostApiAgentDevBlock, /^\s{4}[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*:/gm),
    e2eHelperCount: countMatches(e2eFixture, /export async function (openAgentDevScenario|getAgentDevSnapshot|configureAgentDevHostReplay|getAgentDevHostCalls)/g),
    schemaAssertionCount: countMatches(schemaText, /export function assertAgentDev/g),
  },
  quality: {
    a11yRuleCount: countMatches(a11yText, /add\('([^']+)'/g),
    visualArtifactSpec: existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'tests/e2e/agent-dev-quality.spec.ts')),
    workbenchScript: existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'scripts/agent-dev-workbench.mjs')),
  },
  selectorCoverage: await scanSelectorCoverage(),
  reliability: aggregateReliability(JSON.parse(reliabilityFixtureText)),
  externalTools: [
    { package: '@axe-core/playwright', installed: packageInstalled('@axe-core/playwright'), role: 'strict a11y scanning' },
    { package: '@ladle/react', installed: packageInstalled('@ladle/react'), role: 'component scenario workbench' },
    { package: '@argos-ci/playwright', installed: packageInstalled('@argos-ci/playwright'), role: 'hosted visual regression' },
    { package: '@vitest/browser', installed: packageInstalled('@vitest/browser'), role: 'browser component testing' },
    { package: '@testing-library/user-event', installed: packageInstalled('@testing-library/user-event'), role: 'realistic component interactions' },
    { package: 'knip', installed: packageInstalled('knip'), role: 'unused files/deps/exports' },
    { package: 'ajv', installed: packageInstalled('ajv'), role: 'JSON schema validation engine' },
  ],
};
report.durationMs = Number((performance.now() - start).toFixed(1));

await mkdir(OUT_DIR, { recursive: true });
await writeFile(resolve(OUT_DIR, 'report.json'), JSON.stringify(report, null, 2), 'utf8');
await writeFile(resolve(OUT_DIR, 'report.md'), renderMarkdown(report), 'utf8');
console.log(JSON.stringify(report, null, 2));
"}]}

